.TH FSCK 8 2026-09-25 "Substrate" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fsck \- check a file system (stub)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fsck
.RI [ argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The in-tree
.B fsck
is a placeholder.
It ignores all of its arguments, prints the line
.PP
.EX
fsck: stub implementation
.EE
.PP
to standard output, and exits.
It does not open any device and does not examine or repair any file
system.
.PP
To check an ext2, ext3 or ext4 file system, use
.BR e2fsck (8)
(also installed as
.BR fsck.ext2 ,
.BR fsck.ext3
and
.BR fsck.ext4 )
from the e2fsprogs port.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B fsck
always exits with status 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkfs (8),
.BR e2fsck (8)
.SH BUGS
Not implemented.
Because the exit status is always 0, a script that runs
.B fsck
cannot tell that no check took place.
